{"description":"Priority: P2 | Area: area:network, area:security | Labels: feat | Milestone: v0.1.0 | Task: CTX-0021 | Split from CTX-0016 | Closes umbrella #14.

One TlsConfig vocabulary type (bundle path and/or inline PEM) plus one client-identity policy, wired into BOTH the reqwest rustls client and the tungstenite rustls connector so both trust the same roots. Unset bundle keeps native roots; default is no client certificate. Tests spin a local TLS endpoint with a test-only CA, no network and no committed private keys. mTLS credential storage/redaction needs a security-corpus review note filed with the PR before third-party use (BN-8 gate).

FILE SCOPE WARNING: touches crates/bitty-network/src/http.rs and websocket.rs, which lanes A and B are currently editing. Must not start until CTX-0017 and CTX-0018 merge to main (encoded as dependencies). New deps need deny.toml approval; pure-Rust only.","displayId":"CTX-0021","id":"01M3BN67VQV8G8AGCRF520GGFN","priority":"high","status":"planned","title":"Lane E1: unified TLS provider (CA bundle + mTLS policy) for #21/#22"}

{"description":"Priority: P2 | Area: area:network | Labels: feat | Milestone: v0.1.0 | Task: CTX-0022 | Split from CTX-0016 | Closes umbrella #15 (part).

Two deliverables, both P2 and independent of the TLS lane. (1) #23: one shared TTL cache in the dns module (positive + negative entries, bounded size, per-record deadlines) used by every backend; decide and document where it sits given reqwest resolves internally (cache at our dial layer, or document why http cannot share it). Fake-clock or short-TTL unit tests, no network. (2) #24: one documented proxy precedence (explicit with_proxy override, then environment, then system/PAC) shared by http and websocket; PAC needs an explicit decision first (embedded JS eval vs platform lookup vs unsupported-fail-closed) recorded in the design. Pure-Rust, no OpenSSL; new crates need deny.toml approval.

FILE SCOPE WARNING: dns.rs and proxy.rs are being edited by lane C (CTX-0019). Do not start until CTX-0019 merges to main (encoded as dependency).","displayId":"CTX-0022","id":"01M3BN6CNS36WQYCBZ0PC8GPMA","priority":"high","status":"planned","title":"Lane E2: shared DNS cache + system-proxy/PAC precedence for #23/#24"}

{"description":"Priority: P2 | Area: area:network | Labels: feat | Milestone: v0.1.0 | Task: CTX-0023 | Split from CTX-0016 | RFC: OQ-085 | Closes umbrella #16 (part).

Define the per-plugin per-host audit entry vocabulary in bitty-network-api as types only (allow/deny, host, port, method, timestamp, plugin identity hook) plus a sink trait the host implements; backends call the sink on every check outcome. Bounded memory (no unbounded log growth), no PII beyond host/port. Design the plugin-identity handoff with the bitty host side and record it. Pure-Rust, no network, no new deps without deny.toml approval.

FILE SCOPE WARNING: the api crate and the check-outcome call sites in http.rs/websocket.rs overlap lanes A, B, and E1. Do not start until CTX-0017, CTX-0018, and CTX-0021 merge (encoded as dependencies).","displayId":"CTX-0023","id":"01M3BN6J5WVXAEQXAEGPQ6HR43","priority":"normal","status":"planned","title":"Lane E3: inspector feed audit vocabulary + sink trait for #31"}

{"description":"Priority: P2 | Area: area:network, area:security | Labels: feat | Milestone: v0.1.0 | Task: CTX-0024 | Split from CTX-0016 | Closes umbrella #15 (part).

Single-point authenticated-proxy credential handling shared by http and websocket: one credential source, one injection point, redaction from logs and error strings. Storage and rotation rules need a security-corpus review note filed with the PR before third-party use (BN-8 gate). Until the policy lands, proxies requiring auth keep failing closed (do not weaken this while implementing). Pure-Rust, no new deps without deny.toml approval.

